  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Selgantolimod may interact with Serine hydroxymethyltransferase, cytosolic through a series of intermediate targets. The drug is predicted to target multiple entities, including Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A and Carboxypeptidase N subunit 2, which in turn are targets of Magnesium levulinate. All three of these intermediates are ultimately linked to Serine hydroxymethyltransferase, cytosolic, indicating a potential pathway through which Selgantolimod may exert its effect. The high scores across the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible regulatory or enzymatic role for Selgantolimod in modulating the activity of Serine hydroxymethyltransferase, cytosolic, through a cascade involving Magnesium levulinate."
